  "overview": "**Infor Design System** is a light-first design system anchored on `#f0f0f0` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (17.3:1 contrast) and `#69b5dd` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `System UI` (35px display down to 16px body), unified by `2px` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Infor**. Source: published token package (https://oxford.awsdev.infor.com/infor-design/enterprise), package `ids-enterprise`. Inventory: **91** colors, **9** typography steps, and **40** documented components (Apache-2.0 license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 40 component tokens with documented paddings: `0 10px`, `0`, `0 32px`, `10px 30px`, `10px 20px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f0f0f0` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 0 4px 0 #E0E0E1`, `0 0 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15)`) paired with `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#69b5dd` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#f0f0f0` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#69b5dd` with `#0b0b0c` text (8.7:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `System UI` headings with `System UI` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `2px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (2px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#f0f0f0` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `2px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input-style` fields and secondary buttons."
}
